※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=9
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ The colon stays when the type is left out; the suffix on the value is what
※ the type is taken from.  Written without a space the two characters read
※ as ':=', but they are the same two tokens either way.
@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    var status := 9u8
    status
